{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And you shall see the land, what it is.</b> Whether it is a land settled with many cities and unwalled towns." "<b>And the people that dwell therein.</b> To know whether the settlement of the land is salubrious, as the medical scholars have instructed regarding the selection of dwellings: we should look at the inhabitants of the land, whether they are strong and physically sound, or the opposite. And likewise we should look whether they are many or few, for the multitude and strength of the people indicates that the air of the land and its foods are good, and the opposite indicates their opposite."], :book :numbers, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:39:36.622918318Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}